IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ppl-provisions`

-- Cross-references of the in-scope text (Chapter 2 Parts 2-1 to 2-3 Division 4 and the Dictionary
-- entries for the terms those sections use), one row per cited provision, found by a script that reads
-- the text file: it looks for the words section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, Part, Division,
-- Subdivision, Chapter, Schedule, clause, item and step followed by a number or letter, expands lists
-- ("sections 31AB and 31ABA" is two rows), and resolves a bare "subsection (3)" against the section it sits in.
-- A row of the first kind names a provision of this Act: the identifier it cites, the sub-unit if one is
-- cited, and the heading the index prints for it. A row of the second kind names an Act or instrument and is
-- not resolved here.

DECLARE `Reference within this Act` HAS
    row IS A NUMBER
    `citing provision` IS A STRING
    `citation words` IS A STRING
    `cited identifier` IS A STRING
    `cited unit` IS A STRING
    `cited heading` IS A STRING
    `cited provision is` IS A `Scope of a provision`
    line IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Reference to another Act or instrument` HAS
    row IS A NUMBER
    `citing provision` IS A STRING
    `citation words` IS A STRING
    instrument IS A STRING
    `provision as printed` IS A STRING
    line IS A NUMBER

-- ruler:  row, citing provision, citation words, cited identifier, cited unit (empty when the whole provision is cited), cited heading, scope of the cited provision, line of the text file
@ref Cross-references printed in the in-scope text
`the references within this Act` MEANS
