-- A row is sound when the cited identifier is in the index, the cited sub-unit (if any) is one the index prints for that section,
-- the heading the row carries is the index's heading for it, and the scope the row carries is the index's scope flag.
GIVEN r IS A `Reference within this Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference agrees with the index` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the index entry for` (r's `cited identifier`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p THEN
            p's heading EQUALS r's `cited heading`
        AND p's scope EQUALS r's `cited provision is`
        AND (r's `cited unit` EQUALS "" OR `the index prints the unit` (r's `cited identifier`) (r's `cited unit`))

GIVEN r IS A `Reference to another Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference names an instrument` MEANS
    NOT (r's instrument EQUALS "")

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reference within this Act`
`the reference within this Act numbered` MEANS at `the references within this Act` (n MINUS 1)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reference to another Act or instrument`
`the reference to another instrument numbered` MEANS at `the references to other Acts and instruments` (n MINUS 1)

